# Governs what COPY puts in the image. The heavy collector databases are named explicitly rather than excluding
# `data`, because excluding the directory silently left out data/record.db and the web service deployed with an
# empty archive.
node_modules
data/pump.db*
# data/seed.db is no longer COPYed either; the merge it existed for is done and recorded. Both files have to agree:
# .railwayignore governs what is uploaded, this one governs what COPY puts in the image, and changing one without
# the other is how a deploy came up healthy with the seed simply absent. Re-add `!data/seed.db` to BOTH to seed a
# fresh collector, and remove it from both immediately after.
data/seed.db*
data/archive.db*
data/reports
data/telegram.session
data/*.jsonl
site/t
site/w
site/api/t
site/api/w
.env
.env.bak.*
*.log
